WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:06.210
If I do all of this, uh, my hope is that
at the end of the three months, uh, I

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.850
will have made a significant improvement.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:10.640
Steve Kaufmann here.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:14.990
How do we maintain our commitment
in learning a language?

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.700
That's what I'm going to talk about today.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.620
And I'm going to talk about it in the
context of my next 90-Day Challenge.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.970
Now, remember if you enjoy these
videos, please subscribe, click

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.470
on the bell for notifications.

00:00:28.515 --> 00:00:33.195
Now, you know, I often make the point
that language learning is not a sprint.

00:00:33.405 --> 00:00:36.315
It's a long distance race.

00:00:36.345 --> 00:00:38.355
It's not even a race, it's a journey.

00:00:39.135 --> 00:00:43.004
And there was once, uh, I think
a movie called The Loneliness

00:00:43.035 --> 00:00:44.685
of the Long Distance Runner.

00:00:45.375 --> 00:00:50.295
And so as we're engaged in this long
distance process of learning a language,

00:00:50.325 --> 00:00:53.114
it's easy to see our enthusiasm flag.

00:00:53.415 --> 00:00:57.660
And that's why from time to time,
I join a challenge at LingQ.

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:02.940
And so I'm going to do a 90-Day
Challenge, but I'm going to

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.769
do three different challenges.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:08.910
Now there's a place on LingQ where
it invites you to join a challenge.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:15.240
So I joined the, um, Streak with
Steve challenge, which is where I'm

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:19.770
committed to maintaining my streak,
that I have to save so many LingQs,

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.510
create so many LingQs every day.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:23.920
Um, so that's one.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:28.679
But I'm also going to do a 90-Day
Challenge in Arabic and Persian.

00:01:28.679 --> 00:01:32.070
So it's three challenges, but
it's really the same challenge.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:39.570
What I'm committing to do is to save, to
create a minimum - and I'll go into how I

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:47.130
set these, my goals - but 13 LingQs a day
in Arabic and 13 LngQs a day in Persian.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:53.410
Now the streaks that we track at
LingQ have to do with creating LingQs.

00:01:53.655 --> 00:01:56.235
But that's not my only activity.

00:01:56.625 --> 00:02:01.545
I'm going to be speaking with my tutors
two or three at least times a week.

00:02:02.145 --> 00:02:04.664
One tutor in Arabic, one tutor in Persian.

00:02:05.854 --> 00:02:08.835
I'm going to be doing my
usual reading and listening.

00:02:09.585 --> 00:02:15.975
However, in order to meet my LingQs
target or goal I did a number of things.

00:02:15.975 --> 00:02:21.405
First of all, I adjusted my daily
goal down because I, you know, if

00:02:21.405 --> 00:02:27.705
you go to the settings gear symbol on
LingQ, you can set your daily goal.

00:02:28.125 --> 00:02:32.175
And there's this sort of, you know,
intensive level, which I have done in the

00:02:32.175 --> 00:02:34.065
past, which is a hundred LingQs a day.

00:02:34.745 --> 00:02:38.175
And then there's what we call casual,
which is only 13 LingQs a day.

00:02:39.135 --> 00:02:45.105
And so I adjusted my goals down to 13
because I want to maintain my streak.

00:02:45.614 --> 00:02:51.015
I want to be able to do at least every
day, I want to do 13 saved LingQs in

00:02:51.225 --> 00:02:52.845
at least one of the two languages.

00:02:53.385 --> 00:02:56.234
So that means that I have
to bring in new material.

00:02:57.135 --> 00:03:02.445
I have been in both Arabic and Persian,
I have been spending a lot of time

00:03:02.445 --> 00:03:07.334
with my existing content because I
have so many saved LingQs, especially

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:11.190
in Arabic, words that, you know,
I've, I've looked up, they're now

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.929
yellow, but I still don't know them.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:17.070
So I go back into content that
I've listened to before hoping

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:19.019
to move some of these to known.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.880
The problem with that is the brain
doesn't remember much it seems.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.609
It doesn't remember the
words, but it knows that the

00:03:26.609 --> 00:03:28.410
content is not new any longer.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:29.489
It's heard it before.

00:03:29.579 --> 00:03:30.480
It's read it before.

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:33.420
So it's less stimulating for the brain.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.410
So I'm going to force myself
to bring in new content.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:42.370
Now this could be in the case of
Persian, some of the content that Sahra

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.280
is creating for me in Iran about...

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:47.430
she travels in her country
and this kind of thing.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:47.609
Or

00:03:47.925 --> 00:03:54.275
how about, uh, you know, she's done some
on, on a movie director in Iran, and

00:03:54.275 --> 00:03:56.045
then she sends me a link to the movie.

00:03:56.045 --> 00:04:00.545
So I'm going to try to see if I can
find these Iranian movies somewhere.

00:04:00.545 --> 00:04:02.225
It's not that easy to do.

00:04:02.555 --> 00:04:05.315
And of course the dialogue is very
fast and I don't understand it.

00:04:05.315 --> 00:04:08.285
And we're trying to figure out
how I can maybe extract the

00:04:08.285 --> 00:04:10.505
audio and we're working on that.

00:04:11.454 --> 00:04:16.515
And of course, and with Arabic, uh, what
I want to do is I want to focus more on

00:04:16.935 --> 00:04:18.974
to Arabic so that I can enjoy movies.

00:04:19.005 --> 00:04:21.584
Cause right now I don't
understand the movies and most

00:04:21.584 --> 00:04:22.695
of the movies come from Egypt.

00:04:24.075 --> 00:04:27.705
And for that reason, I've started
talking to Mohammed, who is from Cairo.

00:04:27.765 --> 00:04:30.495
And we started a few lessons
now in Egyptian Arabic.

00:04:30.525 --> 00:04:34.605
I have listened to the mini stories
quite a few times in Egyptian Arabic.

00:04:35.235 --> 00:04:40.110
And so then I get on with Mohammed
and I read a story and then he, and

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:44.240
because the stories consist of, you
know, part A, which is third person

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:48.075
and part b, which is first person
or past tense or future tense.

00:04:48.674 --> 00:04:52.125
And then there are questions where
the answers are sort of provided.

00:04:52.155 --> 00:04:56.114
And so he reads the statement, he
asks me a question and I'm reading

00:04:56.114 --> 00:05:01.455
along and I answer reading along and
he corrects my pronunciation and this

00:05:01.455 --> 00:05:03.255
gets me closer to Egyptian Arabic.

00:05:03.734 --> 00:05:06.075
And I'm hoping that through
this process, I'll be able to

00:05:06.075 --> 00:05:07.784
understand Egyptian movies.

00:05:07.965 --> 00:05:14.130
So if I can continue my sort of input
activities, reading and listening if

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:19.740
I can get on with my tutors, do some
reading and some speaking, if I can access

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:25.710
now movies, which is the live language,
people living the language, over a period

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:31.650
of three months and, but every day I
have to find at least 13 new words that

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:37.920
I save as LingQs and put them into my
vast collection of, of saved LingQs that

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.140
I'm still trying to learn yellow words.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:46.440
If I do all of this, uh, my hope is, uh,
that at the end of the three months, uh, I

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:49.070
will have made a significant improvement.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:53.810
Uh, yeah, the idea of the, of
the challenge is, is, is not

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:57.830
that you're going to necessarily
measure how much better you became.

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:02.390
It is a little nudge to get
you going every day, because

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:03.920
I want to maintain my streak.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.590
I want to save those 13 LingQs.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:09.830
Uh, it's a bit of a commitment and I'm
hoping that other people on LingQ will

00:06:10.125 --> 00:06:12.224
do the same and so we can compare.

00:06:12.284 --> 00:06:14.865
It doesn't mean that everyone
is studying Arabic and Persian.

00:06:15.195 --> 00:06:18.705
People might be studying
Chinese or Russian or Spanish or

00:06:18.705 --> 00:06:20.235
Portuguese or whatever it is...

00:06:20.445 --> 00:06:21.075
english.

00:06:21.525 --> 00:06:23.145
Uh, but at least we're kind...

00:06:23.145 --> 00:06:26.175
of that loneliness of
the long distance runner.

00:06:26.175 --> 00:06:29.685
The loneliness of the
language learner is lessened.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:35.880
To the extent that we can share our
experience, share our activities

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:40.650
and make sure that we maintain
our streaks or, you know, uh,

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:44.370
whatever level we set for ourselves,
goals that we set for ourselves.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:49.710
So we're kind of collectively pushing
each other to work a little harder and

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:54.300
hopefully enjoy it more because the
goal ultimately is to enjoy learning

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.250
the language, not necessarily to,

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:05.219
I dunno, achieve some numerical number,
it's to feel more comfortable, more

00:07:05.219 --> 00:07:07.380
engaged with learning the language.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:12.419
At any rate, that is what I'm going
to do for the next three months.

00:07:12.419 --> 00:07:13.679
It's a 90-Day Challenge.

00:07:13.679 --> 00:07:19.320
I'm going to try to maintain my streak
and I'm going to try to see how far I

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:24.780
can push my, my numbers on my profile
at LingQ, known words and so forth.

00:07:25.335 --> 00:07:28.365
But the only goal I'm going to
really track is to save LingQs.

00:07:28.425 --> 00:07:33.344
That makes it easier for me, eh,
fewer, uh, you know, less pressure.

00:07:34.065 --> 00:07:37.635
Um, I'm going to have these
increased, have this increased

00:07:37.665 --> 00:07:38.805
interaction with my tutors.

00:07:39.195 --> 00:07:44.055
I'm hoping that that will move me into
a situation where I can enjoy movies.

00:07:44.365 --> 00:07:46.625
Then I have to persuade my
wife that we're going to watch

00:07:47.155 --> 00:07:50.970
arabic or person movies rather
than whatever latest thing she's

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.620
found on Netflix or Amazon.

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:58.020
Right now we're enjoying a Danish
movie "By the Seaside" or something

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.730
of that nature from Amazon.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:00.540
It's spectacular.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:01.980
I love listening to Danish.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:04.680
I don't understand it
as well as I would like.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:07.710
Uh, I even ran through our
mini stories in Danish.

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:09.390
I see we only have 25.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:11.310
I would love to have the full set of 60.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:15.240
If there's any Danish people out there
that want to help us with getting more

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:17.745
content into LingQ, please let me know.

00:08:18.705 --> 00:08:24.735
And I encourage all of you to make a
commitment to the next 90-Day Challenge.

00:08:24.795 --> 00:08:25.855
Sign up at LingQ.

00:08:27.105 --> 00:08:27.885
Thank you for listening.

